error[NK1330]: `Names::names` hands back `Vec[winnow_grammar::Symbol]`, which holds a `winnow_grammar::Symbol`, but it isn't handed the table its names are interned into.
   --> tests/grammar_words_required.nika:33:5
    |
 33 |     let a = Names::names(input) catch {
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: Without `words:` the entry interns into a table of its own, which is gone after the call: a symbol it hands back could never be read as text (ADR-388 D2).
    = help: Make a table and hand it over: `let table = winnow_grammar::InternerContext()`, then `Names::names(input; words: table)`; `table.resolve(symbol)` reads a name back.
